**Remediation** (per Shai-Hulud guidance, applies to every exact match):
1. **Isolate the host BEFORE rotating credentials** — many supply-chain payloads include a dead-man switch (`rm -rf ~/` on token revocation).
2. Stop / remove persistence: `systemctl disable --now gh-token-monitor.service pgsql-monitor.service`
3. `npm uninstall` / `pip uninstall` the matched versions
4. Rotate: GitHub tokens, npm tokens, AWS / GCP / Azure creds (IMDSv2 + ECS + SSM), Kubernetes service accounts, HashiCorp Vault tokens, SSH keys, Docker auth, password manager exports
5. Block outbound to the network IOCs listed in each campaign page
6. Rebuild CI/CD runners from clean images
